# TREK React UI

Pages under `client/src/pages` are wiring containers; state, effects, and handlers live in co-located `use<Page>()` hooks (`PATTERN.md`). `npm run lint:pages` enforces this.

Routes live only in `client/src/App.tsx`. Do not add file-based routing or a second router.

## Theme

Use semantic tokens (`bg-surface*`, `text-content*`, `border-edge*`, `bg-accent`). Never raw `bg-slate-*` / `bg-white` for surfaces. Components read CSS tokens; only `applyAppearance()` writes appearance to the DOM. See `client/src/theme/README.md`.

## UX contract

Loading ≠ empty ≠ error ≠ unauthorized. Keep TREK chrome (`trek-nav-pill`, `.atlas`, TripPlanner shell) and show empty/zero/toast rather than deleting structure. Do not fabricate fallback domain data. Do not add fake delays to hide latency. Prefer existing toast helpers.

Default map: Mapbox GL (`VITE_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN`). Keep Leaflet and MapLibre selectable.

## Zustand

Stores live in `client/src/store/`. Subscribe with selectors; use `useShallow` for object picks. Do not dump server/Supabase rows into Zustand unless an existing store already owns that session view. Do not change persisted store shapes without a consumer search. Do not add Redux.

```tsx
export default function DashboardPage() {
  const { t } = useTranslation()
  const { trips, isLoading, handleCreate } = useDashboard()
  if (isLoading) return <Spinner />
  return <Grid trips={trips} onCreate={handleCreate} />
}
```
